  "review": {
    "acl": "Foreign-user CanSearch/CanWrite conservatively include ACL-mask and other-class access. Actual0700 denials remain derived without group-membership-only denial.",
    "metadata": "Authority frames preserve UID, low permission/sticky bits and type only, while bytes, links, size and timestamps remain broad. Fresh mkdir derives physical lifetime/owner/mask from the same source call and actual operation.",
    "native_boundary": "NativeChannelProducer is an application producer obligation: actual native socketpair/dup/file-action/exec evidence must supply EngineChannels on this same handoff. It is not a trusted initial-safe-table axiom, and is not yet instantiated by this supporting record.",
    "profile_extension": "The actual VM and host namespace-passive source predicates now exclude setAttribute and require readFlags or directoryFlags for opens. Actual source proves all arbitrary-reply/loss branches. No kernel hostile transition was removed and runtime is unchanged by this proof-only extension.",
    "remaining": "Actual native producer coupling; global peer family/capability fold and same-birth backing custody; separate backend child steps; source-scoped key/MAC origin; compatible useful model and integrated acceptance.",
    "source": "Every selected actual actor call derives an earlier launch and its exact source-recorded prefix from the same actor journal. Selected source spawns derive successful Startup and raw close-on-exec from individual source/allocation/SDK laws."
  },
